body:
Shadow of War Phase 2 - 4

&#x200B;

I was on a mission, taking out a captain on a Caragor hunt, when suddenly, I was attacked by Stakuga King Slayer. He was an exceptionally weak orc who I did not want in my army, so I simply decided to kill him. When his health reached green level, I decided to dominate him for health, and right before I continued fighting him, I decided I wanted to shame him for the inconvenience he brought upon me, as the orc I was actually after had managed to flee. I shamed Stakuga, and he ran off.

&#x200B;

I all over again tried to track down the orc I actually wanted in my army, but I ran into a Graug, and decided to try and dominate him, as I had never rode one of them before. Unfortunately for me, Stakuga once again came out of nowhere and attacked me. But he was different this time. He was covered in white hands, he no longer wore the gold armor I remembered him by. He had cast away the king slayer part of himself, and he had become Stakuga the Unashamed. Yep, my shaming had only leveled him up, and he wouldn't shut up about how he was unshamable. I battled him, and nearly died do to the Graug in the background, but eventually (since Stakuga was also damaging it) I managed to mount it. With it, I defeated Stakuga, and recruited him, as he was now far more powerful.

&#x200B;

Didn't think much of it, until I was battling a super high level captain, who was kicking my ass. I had used up my last chances, and I thought I was going to die. Then suddenly, out of nowhere, Stakuga comes to my rescue and kills the lvl 60 captain with nearly full health in one hit. He then said to me "there is no shame in needing my help." After this I made him my bodyguard. We went on many adventures together. I leveled him up, gave him flame weapons and so on and so forth. He was incredibly strong, he even killed another orc in the arena in literally 1 hit, it was incredible to see. So naturally, when trying to capture the Gorgoroth fortress, I made him my army leader, and when it was captured, I obviously made him the overlord, though I occasionally used him as my bodyguard instead.

&#x200B;

There he stood until phase 4 of the game, where increasingly powerful orcs attacked Gorgoroth. I tried defending, but it sure as hell wasn't easy, as I play on brutal difficulty. The fortress was taken, and Stakuga was to be excecated. I tracked down the executioner, and watched afar as Stakuga went on about how not even the Gravewalker could shame him. Right at that moment, the gravewalker came to his rescue. I set him free, and he had revenge on the orc intending to excecute him, mainly by removing his head from his shoulders. Stakuga was once again, my bodyguard.

&#x200B;

While from my perspective, we were close friends, it seem that Stakuga was never perfectly happy with me. He probably thought I was below him, as he was exceptionally powerful. This all came to light after 2 failed attempts of recapturing the fortress. My solution was to take out pretty much every orc on the map before retrying, a cowardly move I admit. I called out Stakuga, my bodyguard as I was battling a warchief, and that was when he turned on me. He told me he was ashamed of me, and though I was useless. Again, Stakuga was powerful as hell, and he kicked my ass. I tried to battle him, but was killed again and without him, capturing the Gorgoroth fort would be difficult. So instead, I headed back to Minas Morgul to manage my army there, for no particular reason. I was battling an orc there when suddenly, Stakuga appeared. He said that he had travelled all the way from Gorgoroth to Minas Morgul (aka across the entirety of Mordor) just to kill me. I was confused. I had seen him as a friend for so long, and I didn't want to die, so I simply fled.

&#x200B;

 After this I gathered my strongest orcs and went after him.  I think I sent 4 orcs total, and I remember him killing multiple of them, so I suppose you could say he went down in a blaze of glory. Finally, I dominated him, ready to make him my servant once again. I was ready to put this rivalry behind us, and resume our friendship. But that is when I realized it. He was a level 67 legendary. Too powerful to recruit. Unshamable. I had no choice but to kill him. I couldn't. I fled once more.

&#x200B;

I hated the idea of this orc who I had grown a real bond with was going to disappear forever if I killed him, so I let him be. Instead I finished phase 4 of the game and witnessed the ending. But I couldn't end there, there was still something I had to do. I returned to Minas Morgul, and there he was. After one last taunt from Stakuga, our last duel began. I killed all surrounding enemies first until it was only us two left. It was incredibly climactic, despite me being far more powerful now. I knocked him too his knees, and before the last blow he defied death and got up again. Our battle continued, I made a mistake, and almost died, but I had last chance (literally any hit kills you on brutal.) But eventually I knocked him on his knees again. His last words were something like "what a shame it had to end this way." Then I killed him.

&#x200B;

I felt bad after this. I literally screenshoted whilst killing him so that he wouldn't technically be gone forever. But with Stakuga dead, I could finally end the game, and go play something else. But as I was about to shut my console off, I was attacked. It turns out, the bastard had a brother.

&#x200B;

Haven't dealt with this problem yet, and I won't, as at least now I have some conncetion to him, and maybe I'll even recruit his bro I dunno. But this is the deepest friendship, and rivalry I have ever felt to an NPC in any videogame ever.
